VALUES ('dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 'cpt-practice-5', 'CPT Coding Proficiency Practice Paper 5', 'cpt', ARRAY['Preventive Counseling', 'Ophthalmologic Anesthesia', 'Reconstructive Surgery', 'Bone Densitometry', 'Allergy Lab Testing', 'Psychiatric Therapy', 'MUE Edits']::TEXT[], 100, 'advanced', true, 5, 150);

-- ── Section: Evaluation & Management (20 questions) — Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('6ac63f7e-f6d6-40bd-b6ef-78411d638f1b', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 1, 'Which of the following best describes ''preventive medicine counseling'' codes (individual or group counseling for risk factor reduction, e.g., diet, exercise, substance use, injury prevention), as distinguished from the preventive medicine E/M visit codes already discussed in Paper 1?');
VALUES ('6ac63f7e-f6d6-40bd-b6ef-78411d638f1b', 'c19992cc-9d68-4cb3-a0f2-7f693858986f', 'Preventive counseling/risk-factor-reduction codes are their own distinct family, separate from (though potentially performed alongside) the comprehensive preventive medicine visit codes — reflecting a different service scope (focused counseling vs. comprehensive exam) covering multiple risk-factor topics, not limited to a single subject area.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('17dad97c-d80f-416b-8675-1ac3a7ae2e10', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 2, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for individual preventive counseling versus group preventive counseling (multiple unrelated patients counseled together on a risk-reduction topic)?');
VALUES ('17dad97c-d80f-416b-8675-1ac3a7ae2e10', '42a35d16-f85a-472a-97d3-a3f102939ea1', 'This reapplies the recurring service-structure-determines-code theme (already established for group medical visits and group therapy) to preventive counseling — individual versus group FORMAT is the determining factor, not the specific risk-factor topic being addressed.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('6f549910-cdb9-46f5-bc01-7477137b868c', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 3, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a Welcome to Medicare visit (Initial Preventive Physical Examination, IPPE), as distinguished from a routine annual wellness visit?');
VALUES ('6f549910-cdb9-46f5-bc01-7477137b868c', 'a17b9178-c2f9-4260-9829-68d07ad4e80d', 'The IPPE (one-time, first-year benefit) and the Annual Wellness Visit (recurring, its own initial/subsequent structure) are genuinely distinct Medicare preventive benefit categories with different codes and different frequency/eligibility rules — not interchangeable despite both being ''Medicare preventive visits.''', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('07829dcd-882c-4a1d-afd5-47fc25e72f9f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 4, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a smoking/tobacco use cessation counseling service, as distinguished from general preventive risk-factor counseling?');
VALUES ('07829dcd-882c-4a1d-afd5-47fc25e72f9f', 'b883272c-99c3-464a-9e6e-6e9e7f785bee', 'Smoking/tobacco cessation counseling has its own distinct, time-tiered code family — a specific, high-clinical-priority counseling service warranting its own code structure distinct from the broader general preventive counseling codes.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('b890e179-0b88-4edc-9638-788e19b727cf', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 5, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for alcohol/substance misuse screening and brief intervention services (e.g., SBIRT — Screening, Brief Intervention, and Referral to Treatment)?');
VALUES ('b890e179-0b88-4edc-9638-788e19b727cf', '4e2d6eee-f2d8-4c65-87ba-8f46c3a6cee5', 'SBIRT reflects its own specific, evidence-based service model (screening plus brief intervention) with its own distinct code — different from both a full diagnostic evaluation and general preventive counseling, reinforcing that specific defined SERVICE MODELS (not just general topic area) determine correct code family.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a65f7d2a-48db-4517-98d3-18ee504436fe', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 6, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for obesity screening and counseling (intensive behavioral therapy for obesity), as a specific Medicare-recognized preventive service?');
VALUES ('a65f7d2a-48db-4517-98d3-18ee504436fe', 'a6b60ec1-4c21-4357-9333-183145c1ccfe', 'This reinforces that specific, evidence-based, protocol-defined preventive services (like intensive behavioral therapy for obesity) have their own distinct codes — different from both general preventive counseling and incidental weight discussion during a routine visit, requiring the coder to recognize when the SPECIFIC defined protocol was actually followed.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('c3c10b95-b4c5-4f09-b1c2-75875d3665f4', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 7, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding for time-based preventive counseling services (e.g., smoking cessation, SBIRT, obesity counseling)?');
VALUES ('c3c10b95-b4c5-4f09-b1c2-75875d3665f4', '371750e2-2564-4262-8721-b6dc19cd3280', 'This reinforces the recurring time/protocol-documentation-specificity theme (already established for CCM/PCM/RPM, critical care, and physical therapy) applied to preventive counseling codes specifically — genuine time and protocol-content documentation supports accurate code selection for these defined, evidence-based services.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('9c2bd3ce-6330-40e4-88fc-37449fef5a21', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 8, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when preventive counseling for a specific risk factor (e.g., smoking cessation) is performed during the SAME visit as a problem-oriented E/M service for an unrelated acute complaint?');
VALUES ('9c2bd3ce-6330-40e4-88fc-37449fef5a21', '23192661-022a-4924-b89f-777a7dfb0ed8', 'This reapplies the same-day-multiple-distinct-service principle (already established for preventive visits, ACP, and cardiac rehab combined with E/M) to preventive counseling plus problem-oriented E/M — the same underlying analytical framework, now applied to yet another same-day-combination scenario.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('784ceb26-0e5b-46a6-8ab8-94f9956a37cb', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 9, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for genetic counseling services (e.g., pre-test counseling before genetic testing for a hereditary cancer syndrome), as distinguished from the genetic TESTING itself (already discussed in a prior paper''s Pathology & Laboratory content)?');
VALUES ('784ceb26-0e5b-46a6-8ab8-94f9956a37cb', 'd9291a08-8e73-44ff-b74a-8c7412dad557', 'This connects back to the molecular pathology/genetic testing content from an earlier paper while establishing a distinct point — genetic COUNSELING (a cognitive/discussion service) and genetic TESTING (a laboratory analysis) are different service types, each with its own appropriate code, not conflated into a single code despite being part of the same overall clinical pathway.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0b7b7f6d-168d-406f-b5d0-0277e1aeecc6', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 10, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar E/M-adjacent code-selection question specifically involving preventive counseling services, synthesizing this paper with Papers 1-4?');
VALUES ('0b7b7f6d-168d-406f-b5d0-0277e1aeecc6', '85851106-c4f7-4c3d-8762-a0f76d19f819', 'This is a capstone synthesis for preventive counseling coding — reinforcing, via yet another concrete example, the broader recurring theme that a general category name masks multiple genuinely distinct, specifically-coded service models, requiring identification of the SPECIFIC protocol/format/time actually documented.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('e4529779-1d2d-4467-992f-5da3fba321f5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 11, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a Medicare Annual Wellness Visit (AWV) that also includes an unrelated, medically necessary problem addressed during the same visit (e.g., a new complaint of joint pain)?');
VALUES ('e4529779-1d2d-4467-992f-5da3fba321f5', '59baced1-ecf9-48ab-839f-4b9c3a43c3b7', 'This reapplies the general preventive-visit-plus-distinct-problem coding principle (already established for the general preventive medicine E/M codes in Paper 1) specifically to the Medicare AWV — the AWV''s own defined scope doesn''t include acute problem evaluation, so a genuinely separate, distinct problem may be separately reported alongside it.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f6006172-27ef-4354-8997-e74e950e182f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 12, 'Which of the following best describes the ''health risk assessment'' (HRA) component of a Medicare Annual Wellness Visit?');
VALUES ('f6006172-27ef-4354-8997-e74e950e182f', '0bda5b11-54b9-4434-b4da-64e55968685c', 'The HRA is a required, defined component OF the AWV service itself (not a separate billable add-on, and not IPPE-exclusive) — its completion supports documentation that the AWV''s specific defined scope was actually fulfilled, reinforcing the recurring theme that defined preventive service codes have specific required components.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('9a530268-e730-4784-a485-77f513758f01', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 13, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when a physician performs BOTH an IPPE (Welcome to Medicare visit) AND administers a preventive vaccine (e.g., influenza) during the same visit?');
VALUES ('9a530268-e730-4784-a485-77f513758f01', 'ccaba2e8-8874-4820-a109-8a2009b299d1', 'This connects the vaccine product-plus-administration coding structure (established generally in Paper 1) to the IPPE-specific context — genuinely distinct service components (comprehensive preventive exam vs. immunization) performed at the same visit are each separately coded per their own respective code families.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4e716dcf-37d0-495c-8297-d8118ed251ff', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 14, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for depression screening performed using a standardized tool (e.g., PHQ-9) during a routine office visit?');
VALUES ('4e716dcf-37d0-495c-8297-d8118ed251ff', '2389fd24-d497-44f9-9b2f-2d627073d3bd', 'This illustrates a genuinely nuanced, payer-and-context-dependent coding question (mirroring the earlier honest acknowledgment of nuanced areas rather than oversimplifying) — the correct treatment depends on the applicable code structure and payer policy, not a single universal rule, reinforcing that even common screening tools require this kind of case-specific verification.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a5d39cde-c29a-4c7a-91a0-a3f4c4baab40', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 15, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable compliance consideration for a primary care practice''s billing pattern for Medicare Annual Wellness Visits combined with same-day problem-oriented E/M services (modifier 25)?');
VALUES ('a5d39cde-c29a-4c7a-91a0-a3f4c4baab40', '2e3ba05f-9c9d-4b0f-949e-f55eb7eb9fe5', 'This applies the general modifier-25 compliance-monitoring theme (already established broadly) to a specific, common, and therefore audit-relevant real-world billing pattern (AWV plus same-day E/M) — a reasonable, targeted compliance-review area given how frequently this specific combination occurs in primary care practice.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('d446d5cf-19fd-443d-aac3-f5ffd89a570a', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 16, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a pre-operative clearance E/M visit (evaluating a patient''s fitness for an upcoming elective surgery), as distinguished from the surgeon''s own pre-operative visit within the surgical global period?');
VALUES ('d446d5cf-19fd-443d-aac3-f5ffd89a570a', '21f6681a-debb-48b0-8b6c-24748369b0fb', 'This is an important practical distinction — a DIFFERENT physician''s pre-operative clearance visit is separately billable under standard E/M (or consultation) codes by THAT physician, while the operating surgeon''s OWN pre-operative visit (within the global period) is generally bundled into their surgical global package — not the same billing treatment despite both being ''pre-operative'' visits.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0405595b-f22d-4c94-9654-575215eda4ec', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 17, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support that a pre-operative clearance visit by a non-surgeon physician is genuinely separate, billable work rather than duplicative of the surgeon''s own pre-operative assessment?');
VALUES ('0405595b-f22d-4c94-9654-575215eda4ec', '0c267a07-2114-41c0-b4fd-09fbd4a6ddc4', 'This reinforces the general documentation-supports-distinct-billable-work principle applied to the pre-operative clearance scenario — genuine, independent clinical evaluation by the clearing physician (not simply duplicating or rubber-stamping the surgeon''s assessment) supports that physician''s separate billing.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('573a7d3b-d274-44c2-8090-d1f77aaad664', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 18, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general lesson connecting preventive counseling, Medicare wellness visits, and pre-operative clearance visits as this paper''s E/M-section content, synthesized with the broader E/M themes from Papers 1-4?');
VALUES ('573a7d3b-d274-44c2-8090-d1f77aaad664', '2dfcfe78-060a-428a-8fea-2d8836448790', 'This is the true final E/M capstone synthesis across the entire four-paper series — reinforcing that the core transferable skill is recognizing which SPECIFIC defined service structure applies to each scenario (not defaulting to standard office-visit E/M logic universally), a skill demonstrated across every E/M variation examined throughout this content.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('777f2304-6b11-4af1-a5a7-be79a2069101', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 19, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a nutrition counseling visit provided by a registered dietitian (medical nutrition therapy, MNT), as distinguished from a physician-provided preventive counseling visit?');
VALUES ('777f2304-6b11-4af1-a5a7-be79a2069101', 'fa492bf2-9941-40b9-a32f-365df8164686', 'MNT codes reflect a distinct provider type (registered dietitian) and service scope, structurally separate from physician-delivered E/M/preventive counseling codes — reinforcing that provider type/scope of practice, alongside service structure, is a genuine code-selection-relevant factor.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4f9deb9e-5d02-4e2b-8f19-cbf270d24ca5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 20, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle connecting the many distinct ''counseling and risk-reduction'' code families discussed in this paper (general preventive counseling, smoking cessation, SBIRT, obesity IBT, genetic counseling, MNT) as a synthesis point?');
VALUES ('4f9deb9e-5d02-4e2b-8f19-cbf270d24ca5', '9eb1a869-c7e6-428b-934c-023e7c53c4ef', 'This is a clean synthesis reinforcing the recurring ''shared general descriptor masks multiple distinct specific codes'' theme (already demonstrated for audiology, hernia repair, and other categories) — now applied to the various counseling/risk-reduction service families covered in this section.', 'Evaluation & Management — authored from AMA CPT E/M guidelines covering preventive counseling and risk-factor-reduction codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

-- ── Section: Anesthesia (10 questions) — Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('c43f680f-d1da-4860-ac31-02a563b3c5c8', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 21, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for anesthesia provided for cataract surgery, typically performed under MAC/monitored sedation with local block rather than general anesthesia?');
VALUES ('c43f680f-d1da-4860-ac31-02a563b3c5c8', 'a44829cd-cbf7-4b37-be0c-ed735418800e', 'This reinforces the procedure/region-specific base-code principle applied to ophthalmologic anesthesia — cataract surgery has its own applicable anesthesia code, typically reflecting the lower base-unit complexity of this commonly brief, MAC-based procedure, not defaulting to a major-surgery code or being uncodeable.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('3bcbf516-9ca2-472d-885f-65a323b8fcad', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 22, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when the ophthalmic surgeon (rather than a separate anesthesia provider) personally administers a retrobulbar or peribulbar block for their own cataract surgery?');
VALUES ('3bcbf516-9ca2-472d-885f-65a323b8fcad', '7ee6171c-69f9-418f-9787-0fe6a695f2ac', 'This connects modifier 47 (already introduced in Paper 4) to a concrete ophthalmology scenario — a surgeon personally administering a regional block (not just general anesthesia) for their own case is a scenario modifier 47 is designed to address, appended to the surgical code rather than using a separate anesthesia-section code.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('c55fc0fe-063e-4526-94ac-50a51b867c19', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 23, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for anesthesia provided for strabismus surgery (eye muscle surgery) in a pediatric patient, regarding qualifying circumstances?');
VALUES ('c55fc0fe-063e-4526-94ac-50a51b867c19', '59635fea-5d23-4998-81a0-a9b47bd0c0d6', 'This connects the general extreme-age qualifying circumstances concept (already established) to a concrete pediatric ophthalmology scenario — reinforcing that qualifying circumstances codes apply across specialties whenever their specific documented threshold is genuinely met, not limited to certain procedure types.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('29fc30c0-68c4-46e4-bfeb-2a7caef9fe19', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 24, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for monitored sedation provided by a separate anesthesia provider (not the ophthalmic surgeon) for a routine cataract surgery in a healthy adult patient?');
VALUES ('29fc30c0-68c4-46e4-bfeb-2a7caef9fe19', '87a6b4ad-0ea7-4242-87fc-5bc6da51fce0', 'This clarifies the boundary of modifier 47''s applicability — it specifically addresses surgeon-administered anesthesia; when a SEPARATE anesthesia provider delivers the service (the more common scenario), the standard ophthalmologic anesthesia code is reported without modifier 47, reinforcing accurate understanding of exactly when this modifier does and doesn''t apply.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('febc566a-8248-4330-9887-9e9eaa9e286d', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 25, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding when distinguishing surgeon-administered versus separate-anesthesia-provider-administered anesthesia for an ophthalmologic procedure?');
VALUES ('febc566a-8248-4330-9887-9e9eaa9e286d', '01ff4b90-31fc-43d1-b847-212306a8468a', 'This reinforces the documentation-specificity principle applied to the surgeon-versus-separate-provider anesthesia distinction — clearly identifying WHO administered the anesthesia is the specific documented fact determining correct modifier/code treatment.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('fc254b2b-d0d1-4314-a0eb-3ce5d9454899', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 26, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar Anesthesia-section code-selection question specifically involving ophthalmologic procedures, synthesizing this paper with Papers 1-4?');
VALUES ('fc254b2b-d0d1-4314-a0eb-3ce5d9454899', 'e7fccd0c-94bd-4f2f-b6cc-5c474d2dd6b8', 'This is a further capstone synthesis for anesthesia coding — ophthalmologic anesthesia is a concrete application of the same general framework (base code, physical status, qualifying circumstances, surgeon-vs-provider administration) already established throughout this content, not a wholly separate specialty-specific system.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('ac0890b7-9ecc-49dd-9b93-aff8dda6f37a', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 27, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for anesthesia provided for a dental procedure requiring general anesthesia (e.g., extensive pediatric dental rehabilitation) performed in an operating room/hospital setting?');
VALUES ('ac0890b7-9ecc-49dd-9b93-aff8dda6f37a', '08c41122-74fa-4ba7-8269-d2fe22b2b138', 'This reinforces the broader theme (already established for diagnostic imaging and ECT anesthesia) that anesthesia coding extends across many non-traditional-surgical contexts including dental procedures — each with its own applicable specific code, not a single universal code or an inherent inability to code these scenarios.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f8ea863d-4d0c-43c3-8d06-62ea8e619fb3', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 28, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for anesthesia provided during a bronchoscopy or upper GI endoscopy (procedures already discussed from a Surgery-section coding standpoint) when general anesthesia (rather than moderate sedation by the proceduralist) is used?');
VALUES ('f8ea863d-4d0c-43c3-8d06-62ea8e619fb3', 'df7bed53-81c0-4113-ac21-a1e37db42317', 'This reinforces and cross-references the Paper 1 moderate-sedation-versus-anesthesia-section distinction — when a SEPARATE anesthesia provider delivers general anesthesia/MAC for an endoscopic procedure (rather than proceduralist-administered moderate sedation), the standard Anesthesia-section procedure-specific code applies instead of the moderate sedation code family.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('21fe51ca-a27d-4c7d-a8ad-9883a6b4c716', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 29, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding when an endoscopic procedure could potentially involve EITHER moderate sedation (proceduralist-administered) OR general anesthesia/MAC (separate anesthesia provider), depending on the specific case?');
VALUES ('21fe51ca-a27d-4c7d-a8ad-9883a6b4c716', 'b5ded34a-18d7-4551-8e8b-1090aa67ffde', 'This reinforces the recurring WHO/WHAT documentation-specificity principle (already established for ophthalmology) applied to endoscopic sedation/anesthesia model selection — clear documentation of the actual model used determines which code family correctly applies.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0e107bfa-97ca-4078-81b3-4b992ffadfda', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 30, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable overarching lesson connecting anesthesia coding across surgical, obstetric, pain management, trauma/emergency, ophthalmologic, dental, and endoscopic/procedural sedation contexts, as a final Anesthesia-section synthesis across all five CPT papers?');
VALUES ('0e107bfa-97ca-4078-81b3-4b992ffadfda', 'b239890a-e483-4fc3-9b41-b0d2856b72b9', 'This is the true final Anesthesia-section capstone synthesis across the entire five-paper series — the same core analytical framework (procedure/region, physical status, qualifying circumstances, administering-provider role, and code-family selection) has been demonstrated to apply consistently across every clinical context examined, from general surgery to obstetrics to pain management to ophthalmology to dental to endoscopic sedation.', 'Anesthesia — authored from standard CPT anesthesia section conventions covering ophthalmologic and monitored-sedation scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

