VALUES ('ff0b9440-9ae3-41a1-a0c7-8d6e3178a82f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 31, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for abdominoplasty (tummy tuck) performed for purely cosmetic reasons, as distinguished from panniculectomy (removal of excess abdominal skin/fat) performed for a documented functional/medical indication (e.g., chronic skin infection under a large pannus)?');
VALUES ('ff0b9440-9ae3-41a1-a0c7-8d6e3178a82f', '8f72c06f-f1a4-4a6b-b0ff-01afafedebf1', 'This reapplies the cosmetic-versus-functional-indication coding distinction (already established for septoplasty/rhinoplasty) to abdominal wall procedures — abdominoplasty and panniculectomy are genuinely distinct codes reflecting different surgical goals/indications despite anatomic similarity.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('7066da49-8b59-46ee-855e-414104836994', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 32, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for free flap reconstruction (e.g., a free TRAM or DIEP flap for breast reconstruction, involving microvascular anastomosis), as distinguished from a local/pedicled flap already discussed generally in Paper 2?');
VALUES ('7066da49-8b59-46ee-855e-414104836994', '33f7253e-8c17-4a0e-92db-9fb11f3d2e28', 'This extends the approach/technique-specificity theme to a more complex reconstructive scenario — free flaps (requiring microvascular anastomosis) and local/pedicled flaps (remaining attached to original blood supply) are genuinely different, significantly different-complexity techniques with distinct codes.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a9cc2756-ffb7-4053-858f-c8c80fd67ac1', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 33, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for microvascular anastomosis performed as part of free flap reconstruction, as a potentially separately identifiable component?');
VALUES ('a9cc2756-ffb7-4053-858f-c8c80fd67ac1', 'ca8836c7-16c4-43c2-aae3-b3bec505a043', 'This reapplies the combined-versus-component code-verification discipline to free flap/microvascular reconstruction — requiring the coder to check the SPECIFIC flap code''s own descriptor rather than assuming anastomosis is automatically separately billable or automatically bundled.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('2279b305-7a67-41dc-ae81-3b7b9247cb30', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 34, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for scar revision surgery, as distinguished from the ''complex repair'' wound-closure technique (which can include scar revision as one of its defining elements, already discussed in Paper 2)?');
VALUES ('2279b305-7a67-41dc-ae81-3b7b9247cb30', '529a47da-7ae5-468c-9a8e-c7eb43e6ac72', 'This reinforces that the SAME general technique concept (scar revision) can map to different codes depending on TIMING/CONTEXT (immediate complex-repair-at-time-of-injury vs. delayed, standalone revision procedure) — a nuanced but genuine distinction requiring attention to when and why the revision is being performed.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4ffd79a2-f1e2-4bd8-b4f2-4485e56c79f7', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 35, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for liposuction performed as part of a body contouring procedure, as distinguished from liposuction performed purely for cosmetic fat removal?');
VALUES ('4ffd79a2-f1e2-4bd8-b4f2-4485e56c79f7', '61b2ac49-75f9-417c-9dd8-61a6660246cd', 'This reinforces the anatomic-specificity coding theme applied to liposuction — the SPECIFIC anatomic area(s) actually treated (as documented) determines correct code selection, consistent with how many other procedures throughout this content are coded by specific documented anatomic site.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a557b6a9-7202-4f09-8144-6ca70ba1b060', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 36, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for varicose vein treatment via endovenous ablation (using laser or radiofrequency energy to close a diseased vein), as distinguished from traditional vein stripping/ligation?');
VALUES ('a557b6a9-7202-4f09-8144-6ca70ba1b060', '78c70ff7-aaa5-4472-9a6c-0dabda7754d3', 'This reinforces the approach/technique-specificity theme yet again — endovenous ablation (energy-based, catheter-directed) and traditional surgical stripping/ligation are genuinely different techniques for treating the same general condition (varicose veins), each with distinct codes.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('ded5c4c4-9326-4813-8aaa-0e7ef2389e97', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 37, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when endovenous ablation is performed on multiple, distinct venous segments in the SAME leg during the same session (e.g., great saphenous vein and a separate tributary)?');
VALUES ('ded5c4c4-9326-4813-8aaa-0e7ef2389e97', 'd59aa303-fc8d-4d05-9188-f513d020f289', 'This reapplies the base-code-plus-additional-site add-on structure (already established for spinal fusion and lesion excisions) to endovenous ablation — multiple distinct venous segments treated in the same session may be reflected via base-plus-add-on coding, not artificially combined or restricted to one segment per session.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('607fd1cb-8941-4e07-8bd4-a610a693ae63', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 38, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for sclerotherapy (injection of a sclerosing agent to close smaller varicose or spider veins), as distinguished from endovenous ablation of larger veins?');
VALUES ('607fd1cb-8941-4e07-8bd4-a610a693ae63', '79b14522-76d1-4468-9919-1d8e48f4138c', 'This further reinforces the technique-specificity theme within venous disease treatment — sclerotherapy (chemical) and endovenous ablation (energy-based) are genuinely different techniques, typically for different vein types/sizes, each with its own distinct code.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('7ab13e37-e183-4841-8341-7211a43c80f9', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 39, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for amputation of a lower extremity at the below-knee level, as distinguished from an above-knee amputation already implicitly discussed generally in earlier ICD-10-PCS-adjacent content?');
VALUES ('7ab13e37-e183-4841-8341-7211a43c80f9', 'ab391e69-300d-44c9-9786-7624d017ce35', 'This reinforces the anatomic-level-specificity theme (already established for the ICD-10-PCS Detachment root operation) applied to CPT amputation coding specifically — both code sets require documenting the SPECIFIC level of amputation, not a single generic code regardless of level.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('ad908017-9516-4a67-b1a5-f782f83a23b2', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 40, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for revision of an amputation stump (e.g., due to poor healing or neuroma formation), as distinguished from the original amputation procedure?');
VALUES ('ad908017-9516-4a67-b1a5-f782f83a23b2', 'bccd7731-c86c-4d31-b4cd-bef48bb96a29', 'This reinforces, once again, the pervasive original-procedure-versus-later-revision coding distinction — a genuinely recurring, transferable theme now demonstrated across an extensive range of procedure/device types throughout this five-paper series.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('bf70c6bd-fa05-4a63-81e1-52b13105a98a', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 41, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a below-knee amputation performed with immediate post-operative prosthetic fitting (a specific surgical technique/protocol), as distinguished from a standard amputation followed by delayed prosthetic fitting at a later date?');
VALUES ('bf70c6bd-fa05-4a63-81e1-52b13105a98a', 'fa116a48-059f-4b43-b229-9dfca10c9c66', 'This reinforces the general ''match the specific documented protocol/technique to the correct code'' principle applied to a nuanced amputation-technique scenario — when a specific technique-matching code exists and was actually performed, it should be used rather than defaulting to a more generic code.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0f8011c6-fd13-4798-acd9-3c3d4b18c146', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 42, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a below-the-knee popliteal-to-tibial arterial bypass graft, as distinguished from a coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) already discussed generally?');
VALUES ('0f8011c6-fd13-4798-acd9-3c3d4b18c146', 'dd58d806-8e26-48a7-a339-c6b4a8d11c0b', 'This reinforces that shared underlying CONCEPT (bypass/rerouting blood flow) doesn''t mean shared codes across different anatomic territories — peripheral arterial bypass and CABG are anatomically distinct procedures with their own specific code families, despite the conceptual similarity.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('aefed7da-5e80-47ec-b474-e7d4ec94fb7d', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 43, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for peripheral arterial bypass graft coding, specifically regarding graft material/conduit type (e.g., autologous vein vs. synthetic graft)?');
VALUES ('aefed7da-5e80-47ec-b474-e7d4ec94fb7d', 'e6abf38a-4e93-4e4a-a66a-00fc9364f18f', 'This reapplies the CABG graft-material/qualifier-specificity principle to peripheral arterial bypass — the same underlying documentation-specificity requirement (conduit type) applies across different anatomic bypass procedure families, not limited to coronary bypass alone.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('85649a7e-ff5e-40c7-a93a-6879b1194ee0', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 44, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a carotid endarterectomy (removal of atherosclerotic plaque from the carotid artery to prevent stroke)?');
VALUES ('85649a7e-ff5e-40c7-a93a-6879b1194ee0', 'f5eec104-5db0-4b94-91e9-f33fdcc13f40', 'This reinforces the technique-specificity theme applied to carotid disease treatment — endarterectomy (open surgical plaque removal) and stenting (endovascular, already conceptually covered in Paper 3''s interventional radiology content) are genuinely different techniques for the same clinical goal, each with distinct codes.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('683ef713-9494-46d3-ab89-fcf7e89562bf', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 45, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for an aortic aneurysm repair performed via endovascular technique (EVAR, endovascular aneurysm repair) versus open surgical repair?');
VALUES ('683ef713-9494-46d3-ab89-fcf7e89562bf', '4539dafb-a42e-4a18-8f31-6d5bbb0915de', 'This reinforces the approach-specificity theme with a significant, high-acuity vascular surgery example — EVAR (endovascular) and open surgical aneurysm repair represent fundamentally different techniques with distinct codes, despite treating the same underlying condition.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f2995fa2-6ca5-4124-b368-0bb1e565ae06', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 46, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar Surgery-section code-selection question specifically involving plastic/reconstructive or vascular surgery procedures, as the final Surgery-section synthesis across this entire five-paper series?');
VALUES ('f2995fa2-6ca5-4124-b368-0bb1e565ae06', '45fba898-8ce3-4588-b026-5064465b4687', 'This is the true final Surgery-section capstone synthesis for the entire five-paper series — reinforcing, via plastic/reconstructive and vascular surgery as the final concrete examples, the single consistent analytical framework (indication, approach, anatomy, device/material, bundling structure) that has been demonstrated to apply across every surgical specialty covered throughout this content.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('93d1c225-f69c-4009-9494-2fd557bf7757', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 47, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a rhytidectomy (facelift) performed for cosmetic purposes, as distinguished from a reconstructive facial procedure following trauma or tumor resection?');
VALUES ('93d1c225-f69c-4009-9494-2fd557bf7757', '8894c3e9-f45e-475c-b2cd-cd923a329235', 'This extends the cosmetic-versus-functional/reconstructive coding distinction (already established for nasal and abdominal procedures) to facial plastic surgery — a recurring, transferable principle across multiple anatomic regions.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('22524db1-9d4e-4216-a9d3-7208e28b5325', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 48, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for blepharoplasty (eyelid surgery), specifically regarding the distinction between a functional indication (e.g., visual field obstruction from excess upper eyelid skin) versus a purely cosmetic indication?');
VALUES ('22524db1-9d4e-4216-a9d3-7208e28b5325', 'fe312a2f-68f5-4daf-8f8f-ff319b9dbdcb', 'This applies the cosmetic-versus-functional coding/coverage distinction to a concrete, commonly-encountered example (blepharoplasty) — genuine functional indication (often requiring specific supporting documentation like visual field testing) supports different coding/coverage treatment than a purely cosmetic indication for the same general procedure.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('16e0229b-5853-4d78-8165-3cc8467a94a0', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 49, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support that a blepharoplasty is functionally (not merely cosmetically) indicated?');
VALUES ('16e0229b-5853-4d78-8165-3cc8467a94a0', 'f6d8dac5-e5fd-4a64-b421-d8a924364cd4', 'This reinforces the general documentation-supports-medical-necessity theme (already established broadly throughout this content) applied specifically to blepharoplasty — genuine objective supporting evidence, not a subjective cosmetic complaint alone, distinguishes functional from cosmetic indication.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('dbe768ff-f97e-4af6-a809-3bfbe5f3a6e0', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 50, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for otoplasty (ear surgery to correct prominent/protruding ears), typically performed in pediatric patients?');
VALUES ('dbe768ff-f97e-4af6-a809-3bfbe5f3a6e0', '4ea65b8e-00a8-4442-8145-538f7cf374bc', 'This extends the cosmetic-versus-functional/coverage-policy analysis to otoplasty — a procedure genuinely subject to payer-specific coverage determination based on documented indication, similar to other plastic surgery procedures already discussed.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('2a12876f-7485-4770-848f-4a35fdab4e84', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 51, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for gender-affirming surgical procedures (e.g., chest reconstruction, genital reconstruction), regarding code selection principles?');
VALUES ('2a12876f-7485-4770-848f-4a35fdab4e84', '85a36317-fb5c-41fd-907b-beb97e63b1fa', 'This reinforces that CPT code selection is fundamentally driven by the SPECIFIC anatomic procedure/technique actually performed (the same codes used for analogous procedures performed for other indications), not a separate code set tied to the clinical context/indication itself — consistent with the procedure-specificity principle established throughout this content.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('1c09c863-d9d0-4ea4-941c-c9600e7534b3', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 52, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice specific to gender-affirming surgical procedures, given that the same anatomic CPT codes may apply as for other indications?');
VALUES ('1c09c863-d9d0-4ea4-941c-c9600e7534b3', '3d97d313-ebad-4982-82c9-05d207db7895', 'This reinforces that procedure-code selection (based on what was anatomically/technically performed) and coverage/medical-necessity determination (based on applicable payer policy) are related but analytically distinct questions — both requiring their own appropriate documentation, consistent with how this distinction has been treated for other procedures throughout this content (e.g., cosmetic vs. functional analysis).', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('15f967e6-dcfc-4077-a7b5-cd86472098d5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 53, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for burn scar reconstruction using tissue expansion (already discussed generally for breast reconstruction) applied to a different body region (e.g., scalp or extremity burn scar)?');
VALUES ('15f967e6-dcfc-4077-a7b5-cd86472098d5', '724fb5a2-3ebb-4df8-86cf-c1cf3401d404', 'This reinforces that a general TECHNIQUE concept (staged tissue expansion) can apply across multiple anatomic regions, while the SPECIFIC code used still depends on the actual anatomic region being treated — the technique concept generalizes, but code selection remains anatomically specific.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('8a2581bb-6f1b-4e67-b42d-e72d812305f4', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 54, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for skin substitute/cellular tissue product application to a chronic wound (e.g., a diabetic foot ulcer that hasn''t responded to standard debridement/wound care)?');
VALUES ('8a2581bb-6f1b-4e67-b42d-e72d812305f4', 'ec9e74dd-5c5c-4a0f-ba05-f39d03b57050', 'This introduces skin substitute/cellular tissue products as their own distinct, specifically-coded advanced wound care category — different from both standard debridement (already covered) and traditional autograft/allograft skin grafting (already covered), reinforcing the recurring theme that related-but-distinct techniques within a broad category (wound care) each warrant their own specific code.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('68983391-787e-4191-b59a-9df20f0e7014', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 55, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when standard excisional debridement is performed at the same session as, and immediately preceding, skin substitute application to prepare the wound bed?');
VALUES ('68983391-787e-4191-b59a-9df20f0e7014', 'a37c4942-04d1-4834-9588-76fc29410d16', 'This reapplies the general genuinely-distinct-components separate-reportability principle (already established for excision-plus-repair, debridement-plus-VAC, and other multi-component wound care scenarios) to debridement-plus-skin-substitute-application specifically.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0dcedcde-436a-44ec-9daa-ac6e08fdcdb4', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 56, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable compliance consideration for a wound care practice''s use of skin substitute/cellular tissue products, given their typically high per-unit cost?');
VALUES ('0dcedcde-436a-44ec-9daa-ac6e08fdcdb4', '25571ce3-a62b-4119-8980-d3df2bc1014c', 'This connects the product-plus-procedure coding structure to a real, documented compliance-risk area (high-cost skin substitute products have drawn genuine OIG/payer scrutiny) — reinforcing the recurring medical-necessity-documentation and targeted-compliance-review themes established throughout this content, applied to this specific, cost-significant category.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0f2e8ed1-92b3-4195-a748-4d701497459c', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 57, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for negative pressure wound therapy (wound VAC, already discussed in Paper 1) applied specifically to a post-surgical incision (incisional NPWT) as a preventive measure, as distinguished from wound VAC applied to an open, chronic wound?');
VALUES ('0f2e8ed1-92b3-4195-a748-4d701497459c', 'b496b8ee-8d00-419e-9c1f-f246d62f2255', 'This extends the wound VAC discussion (Paper 1) with a nuanced distinction (closed-incision preventive use vs. open-wound therapeutic use) — reinforcing the recurring ''verify the specific code structure rather than assume identical treatment'' discipline for what might appear to be the same general technology used in different clinical contexts.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('bf2b4f73-00e2-4436-ad75-1e8b1586ef43', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 58, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a split-thickness skin graft harvested from a donor site, specifically regarding whether the donor site itself requires separate coding consideration?');
VALUES ('bf2b4f73-00e2-4436-ad75-1e8b1586ef43', 'd33afddb-b75a-4c7c-b95b-8fa4847fe36b', 'This reinforces careful attention to the specific scope of a graft code''s own descriptor and applicable guidelines regarding donor-site management — generally understood as part of the overall procedure, but not something to assume without checking the specific code''s own defined scope, consistent with the broader descriptor-verification discipline.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('8b511ac2-2fad-4e3f-9a40-18c8528622a9', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 59, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general lesson from examining cosmetic-versus-functional coding distinctions across nasal surgery, abdominoplasty/panniculectomy, blepharoplasty, otoplasty, and facial plastic surgery throughout this content?');
VALUES ('8b511ac2-2fad-4e3f-9a40-18c8528622a9', 'a2019f4c-f5fc-45e4-b83a-19ffa7e76eea', 'This is a genuine cross-topic synthesis — the cosmetic-versus-functional analytical question recurs across many different anatomic regions/procedures (nose, abdomen, eyelids, ears, face) throughout this content, reinforcing it as a general coding/coverage PRINCIPLE rather than a rule specific to any single procedure type.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('7157a7d9-c661-4de8-b60c-b2f6a6c73fa5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 60, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for revision of a previous cosmetic procedure that develops a genuine medical complication (e.g., infection, implant rupture requiring removal)?');
VALUES ('7157a7d9-c661-4de8-b60c-b2f6a6c73fa5', '855cd205-0c2e-4e62-90f7-72bf7c6266ec', 'This is a nuanced but important distinction — an ORIGINAL cosmetic procedure''s coverage status doesn''t necessarily determine the coverage/coding of a SUBSEQUENT genuine medical complication (infection, implant rupture) requiring treatment, which is evaluated on its own current medical-necessity merits, not automatically inheriting the original procedure''s cosmetic/non-covered status.', 'Surgery — authored from standard CPT Surgery section conventions covering plastic/reconstructive and additional vascular surgery scenarios; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

-- ── Section: Radiology (10 questions) — Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('f40b4c6c-a8f7-4bd2-b427-d886c0414428', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 61, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a DEXA bone density study of the axial skeleton (spine and hip) versus a peripheral DEXA study (e.g., heel or forearm)?');
VALUES ('f40b4c6c-a8f7-4bd2-b427-d886c0414428', '1be2f469-c38e-4eb5-8b83-6b8cc2d30ee0', 'This reinforces the anatomic-site-specificity theme applied to bone densitometry — axial (spine/hip) and peripheral (heel/forearm) DEXA studies serve different clinical purposes and have distinct codes, not a single universal bone density code regardless of site.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('fe5ae80f-7f10-4ad2-96fd-a2d3c3eb48fc', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 62, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for vertebral fracture assessment (VFA) performed as part of, or alongside, a DEXA bone density study?');
VALUES ('fe5ae80f-7f10-4ad2-96fd-a2d3c3eb48fc', 'e0989431-120d-425f-9ad0-7a5393b83f11', 'VFA is a distinct diagnostic assessment (specifically evaluating for vertebral compression fractures) with its own code, separate from standard bone density measurement — reinforcing that even services performed using the SAME equipment/visit can represent genuinely distinct, separately-coded diagnostic purposes.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('49418a72-9342-47f1-ace7-634f8728cb66', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 63, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for fluoroscopic guidance used during a joint injection (e.g., a hip or shoulder injection for diagnostic/therapeutic purposes)?');
VALUES ('49418a72-9342-47f1-ace7-634f8728cb66', '8fee8215-249e-4096-882c-98d2822dfa33', 'This reapplies the recurring imaging-guidance bundling analysis to fluoroscopically-guided joint injections — the same code-descriptor-specific verification discipline already established for other image-guided procedures throughout this content.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f7f645de-6549-4cea-a3cf-15a345f98d91', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 64, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for fluoroscopic guidance used during a lumbar puncture (already discussed generally in this paper''s Surgery-section content), as distinguished from a lumbar puncture performed without imaging guidance (e.g., using anatomic landmarks alone)?');
VALUES ('f7f645de-6549-4cea-a3cf-15a345f98d91', '4de18975-9ad5-4e20-8f86-16dc21332386', 'This connects the lumbar puncture procedure (already discussed) with the imaging-guidance-bundling analysis — whether guidance was actually used and documented is a genuine, code-relevant detail, not an assumption in either direction.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('96afa3a0-3447-4ae2-9e34-d0477f99946b', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 65, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a fluoroscopically-guided arthrogram (contrast injection into a joint under fluoroscopic guidance, followed by imaging), as distinguished from the MRI arthrogram already discussed?');
VALUES ('96afa3a0-3447-4ae2-9e34-d0477f99946b', 'dc51b891-05ed-4afd-8e40-21a263f8e322', 'This extends the arthrography discussion by introducing modality choice (fluoroscopic/plain-film vs. MRI, already discussed) as an additional code-selection factor — reinforcing that the SPECIFIC subsequent imaging modality (not just ''an arthrogram was performed'') determines correct code selection.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f3a92074-1a08-439a-a56a-51b0c9e8a585', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 66, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a fluoroscopically-guided myelogram (already discussed generally regarding CT myelography) using PLAIN FILM (rather than CT) imaging following the contrast injection?');
VALUES ('f3a92074-1a08-439a-a56a-51b0c9e8a585', '87e4dc7b-b728-4abe-bdcb-c17d66e79aad', 'This reinforces the myelography modality-specificity theme (already introduced for CT myelogram) by adding plain-film as an alternative subsequent-imaging-modality option — the same underlying principle (subsequent modality choice affects code selection) applied more completely.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('0e0b8d28-d5c2-4276-ba02-b53c4e7395c5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 67, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding for fluoroscopically-guided procedures generally (joint injections, lumbar puncture, arthrography, myelography), synthesizing the guidance-related themes established throughout this content?');
VALUES ('0e0b8d28-d5c2-4276-ba02-b53c4e7395c5', '860c3069-ec6b-40dc-aecb-52af4f0db485', 'This is a capstone synthesis of the imaging-guidance-bundling documentation theme — explicitly naming both risks (under-reporting a legitimately separate service, and over-reporting/double-billing bundled guidance) reinforces why code-specific verification (not a default assumption in either direction) is the correct, careful approach.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('2b73e7de-7aeb-4f63-b3ce-0538bbd67f7e', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 68, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for a diagnostic X-ray of a specific joint (e.g., knee) performed with weight-bearing views, as distinguished from standard non-weight-bearing views?');
VALUES ('2b73e7de-7aeb-4f63-b3ce-0538bbd67f7e', '2bcea9a4-09d6-4afe-a3d0-3adc1497e35d', 'This reinforces the protocol-specificity theme (already established for contrast timing, functional vs. structural purpose) with an additional example — weight-bearing status is a documented protocol detail potentially relevant to correct code selection for certain joint imaging studies.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4c98cb51-475c-436a-b57c-4b0efc7b6692', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 69, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle connecting the recurring ''protocol/technique specificity beyond just body part and modality'' theme demonstrated across contrast timing, functional vs. structural purpose, guidance modality, and weight-bearing status throughout this content''s Radiology-section coverage?');
VALUES ('4c98cb51-475c-436a-b57c-4b0efc7b6692', '45747210-7444-4a0c-b11c-5ed23a9db8a5', 'This is a genuine capstone synthesis for the entire Radiology-section content across all five papers — the recurring theme (protocol/technique specificity beyond basic body-part-and-modality) is a single, transferable underlying principle, not a series of isolated, unrelated quirks, and it applies across imaging types from plain film through advanced modalities.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('086026a2-6612-41a0-a770-6c69155ac99f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 70, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar Radiology-section code-selection question of ANY type, as the final Radiology-section synthesis across this entire five-paper CPT series?');
VALUES ('086026a2-6612-41a0-a770-6c69155ac99f', 'd2c5ca65-763a-4512-a4a5-bab914ff658c', 'This is the comprehensive, true final Radiology-section capstone synthesis for the entire five-paper series — systematically consolidating every protocol-specificity factor examined throughout this content (modality, anatomy, contrast, specialized purpose, guidance-bundling, and other protocol details) into a single, transferable analytical checklist for accurate radiology code selection.', 'Radiology — authored from standard CPT Radiology section conventions covering bone densitometry and fluoroscopy; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

-- ── Section: Pathology & Laboratory (10 questions) — Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('3df4bd79-ed6a-4002-90b5-b8a88fefe27b', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 71, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for allergen-specific IgE blood testing (e.g., a RAST-type test measuring IgE antibodies to specific allergens), as distinguished from skin prick allergy testing (already implicitly distinguished from immunotherapy in Paper 1)?');
VALUES ('3df4bd79-ed6a-4002-90b5-b8a88fefe27b', '6aebfd83-5818-4300-bba3-71495378bf5c', 'This reinforces both the technique-specificity theme (blood-based vs. skin-based testing being genuinely different methods) and the units-based multi-analyte coding structure (already seen for toxicology and other testing) applied to allergen-specific IgE testing.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('315e28de-421b-4de6-9602-a805d5b2c25c', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 72, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for total serum IgE testing, as distinguished from allergen-SPECIFIC IgE testing?');
VALUES ('315e28de-421b-4de6-9602-a805d5b2c25c', '9039823a-62ba-4d7c-bf67-fc2a7ae5ae24', 'This reinforces the distinct-analyte-distinct-code principle (already established broadly) applied to IgE testing specifically — total IgE (overall level) and allergen-specific IgE (reactivity to particular substances) are genuinely different measurements despite sharing the same antibody class, each with its own code.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('b2a80e33-f89c-406b-9f87-0fe25d00745d', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 73, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for an immunoglobulin panel measuring IgG, IgA, IgM, and IgE levels together, as distinguished from ordering only one of these immunoglobulin classes?');
VALUES ('b2a80e33-f89c-406b-9f87-0fe25d00745d', '9c4ac98b-07e6-4fcb-8b0e-7dc29110c7be', 'This reapplies the panel-completeness principle (already demonstrated for BMP/CMP, thyroid panels, and lipid panels) to immunoglobulin panels — the same general laboratory-panel-coding rule, now confirmed to apply to yet another panel type.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('c560d5c8-ced1-40a1-9bc5-e49a00fe59b3', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 74, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for autoimmune antibody testing (e.g., ANA — antinuclear antibody — testing for suspected lupus or other autoimmune conditions), as distinguished from allergy-specific IgE testing?');
VALUES ('c560d5c8-ced1-40a1-9bc5-e49a00fe59b3', '34e29f99-6428-470a-bd0d-b3ef7674a855', 'This reinforces the recurring ''broad shared category (antibody testing) contains multiple genuinely distinct, specifically-coded test types'' theme — ANA (autoimmune) and allergen-specific IgE (allergic) serve entirely different clinical purposes and have entirely distinct codes despite the shared general ''antibody test'' descriptor.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('7f0bab2d-4e5c-4c70-91ed-dfc5d79f3994', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 75, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when an ANA test returns positive, triggering reflex testing for specific autoimmune antibody subtypes (e.g., anti-dsDNA, anti-Smith antibodies)?');
VALUES ('7f0bab2d-4e5c-4c70-91ed-dfc5d79f3994', 'eded115b-5d6b-4b25-80da-78a83b9f7f06', 'This reapplies the reflex-testing coding principle (already established generally, and specifically for cytology/ASC-US-HPV) to autoimmune antibody testing — confirming this as a truly general laboratory-coding principle applicable across many different testing contexts, not limited to the specific examples where it was first introduced.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('7275aad6-2564-4320-b64e-7fc32c51e6a7', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 76, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for complement level testing (e.g., C3, C4), used to evaluate certain autoimmune or immunodeficiency conditions, as distinguished from immunoglobulin level testing?');
VALUES ('7275aad6-2564-4320-b64e-7fc32c51e6a7', '25dd3d10-8f78-4710-8053-f407206f1028', 'This reinforces the distinct-analyte-distinct-code principle applied to complement testing — genuinely different immunologic parameters (complement proteins vs. immunoglobulins) each warrant their own specific codes, continuing the broader pattern established throughout Pathology & Laboratory content.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('e5c6ab08-6c3d-4475-9dc6-67d3fc64bffc', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 77, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for HLA (human leukocyte antigen) typing, performed for transplant compatibility matching (connecting to the transplant content already discussed generally)?');
VALUES ('e5c6ab08-6c3d-4475-9dc6-67d3fc64bffc', '517ee221-4457-4729-a914-2086dc32195c', 'This connects to the earlier transplant/donor-source content while introducing HLA typing as its own distinct, specialized laboratory test category — reinforcing that specialized clinical purposes (transplant matching) warrant their own specific codes, distinct from general immunology/autoimmune testing.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('c62d66b6-e749-4a0e-b4f8-f07f816681fd', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 78, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding for immunology/allergy testing scenarios (specific allergen panels, immunoglobulin panels, autoimmune reflex testing, HLA typing), synthesizing the recurring Pathology & Laboratory documentation themes established throughout this content?');
VALUES ('c62d66b6-e749-4a0e-b4f8-f07f816681fd', 'f946654a-2f7c-4e5d-9492-131527a826df', 'This is a capstone synthesis applying the recurring Pathology & Laboratory documentation-specificity theme (already established across panels, reflex testing, toxicology, and endocrine testing) to immunology/allergy testing specifically — the same underlying principle, demonstrated now across every major Pathology & Laboratory subsection covered in this five-paper series.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4c747388-d483-4883-8792-1817df440bdc', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 79, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable compliance consideration for a facility''s allergy/immunology testing patterns, given the potential for broad, non-targeted ''shotgun'' allergy panels to be ordered regardless of specific clinical suspicion?');
VALUES ('4c747388-d483-4883-8792-1817df440bdc', '0ac55fd7-9074-44f9-ad31-7017d779bdde', 'This reapplies the medical-necessity/targeted-testing compliance principle (already established for toxicology testing patterns) to allergy/immunology testing — reinforcing this as a general laboratory-testing compliance theme, not limited to the single context where it was first introduced.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('8d126407-6566-438b-9830-f2cf53e44b87', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 80, 'Which of the following best describes the single most important overarching lesson for Pathology & Laboratory CPT coding, as the true final synthesis across the entirety of this five-paper series'' Pathology & Laboratory content (panels, microbiology, cytology, molecular pathology, toxicology, endocrine/tumor markers, and immunology/allergy)?');
VALUES ('8d126407-6566-438b-9830-f2cf53e44b87', '0bf21e1f-607b-427b-a85b-1025345d435e', 'This is the true final Pathology & Laboratory capstone synthesis for the entire five-paper series — the same disciplined analytical approach (specific analyte/methodology verification against defined code scope) and the same medical-necessity/compliance principle apply consistently across every laboratory subsection covered, from routine chemistry panels through specialized immunology testing.', 'Pathology & Laboratory — authored from standard CPT Pathology & Laboratory section conventions covering immunology/allergy testing; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

-- ── Section: Medicine (10 questions) — Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('d969ec2a-a618-4905-94c5-97b42e73f8b7', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 81, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for individual psychotherapy sessions of different documented durations (e.g., 30 minutes versus 45 minutes versus 60 minutes)?');
VALUES ('d969ec2a-a618-4905-94c5-97b42e73f8b7', 'f13f7952-921a-44f8-b7be-29d272d5c9af', 'This reinforces the time-documentation-specificity theme applied to individual psychotherapy — genuine session-duration documentation directly determines which of the time-tiered codes is correctly selected, not a single universal code or duration mattering only for payment amount rather than code selection itself.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f08f8a0d-094f-419b-8f1e-91f379559eb6', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 82, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for family psychotherapy WITH the patient present, as distinguished from family psychotherapy WITHOUT the patient present?');
VALUES ('f08f8a0d-094f-419b-8f1e-91f379559eb6', 'dc45a09f-b7db-42e8-a11b-6f439de67189', 'This reinforces the participant-structure-affects-code-selection theme (already established for split/shared visits and group visits) applied to family psychotherapy — patient presence/absence is the determining factor between these two distinct codes, not session duration alone.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('22e3aa0a-a752-44af-ac2b-f108c27872a6', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 83, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for group psychotherapy, as distinguished from individual psychotherapy and from the interdisciplinary care conference/group medical visit concepts already discussed?');
VALUES ('22e3aa0a-a752-44af-ac2b-f108c27872a6', 'ba75c1dd-8876-4f7b-b8cc-b4e166c20186', 'This reinforces both the participant-structure theme (group vs. individual) and the content-specificity theme (psychotherapeutic vs. general medical) — group psychotherapy is genuinely distinct from both individual psychotherapy and general group medical visits, warranting its own specific code.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('e3dd16e6-f5e8-4314-ba6b-c4eec5a35ba5', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 84, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for psychotherapy for crisis (an urgent, time-based psychotherapy service for a patient in crisis, e.g., acute suicidal ideation), as distinguished from routine scheduled psychotherapy?');
VALUES ('e3dd16e6-f5e8-4314-ba6b-c4eec5a35ba5', '462e497c-5fc9-49bc-9b11-66e55f7652f2', 'This parallels the critical-care coding concept (a specialized, urgent, time-based service with its own base-plus-add-on time structure) applied to psychiatric crisis intervention — reinforcing that urgent/crisis clinical scenarios across different specialties (medical critical care, psychiatric crisis) often warrant their own distinct, time-based code structures.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('58badb92-5faf-49cf-8c01-4a9c1aaf91b6', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 85, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable documentation practice to support correct coding for psychotherapy for crisis, given its time-based structure?');
VALUES ('58badb92-5faf-49cf-8c01-4a9c1aaf91b6', '55ac462e-35b9-40b4-897e-5e8955fb977c', 'This reinforces the recurring time-documentation principle applied specifically to crisis psychotherapy — genuine documented duration (not merely noting that a crisis occurred) supports correct base/add-on code selection, consistent with the pattern established for critical care and other time-based services.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('ee3e8910-cdc6-49e8-8cf1-fcd2fb8f1e1f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 86, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for psychotherapy provided via telehealth, connecting the telehealth E/M concepts (Paper 2) with psychotherapy coding specifically?');
VALUES ('ee3e8910-cdc6-49e8-8cf1-fcd2fb8f1e1f', 'fd9e7f2b-9376-46d0-9c3d-4f49429dd3f7', 'This connects the general telehealth-modifier concept (already established for E/M services) to psychotherapy coding specifically — the same underlying psychotherapy codes apply regardless of delivery modality, with the telehealth-specific modifier/POS indicator reflecting how the service was delivered, not changing which base code applies.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a99dcb9a-63d0-4ccc-a366-7203f9446eb1', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 87, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when a psychiatrist provides both medication management (an E/M service) AND individual psychotherapy during the same visit, using the add-on psychotherapy codes already discussed in Paper 1?');
VALUES ('a99dcb9a-63d0-4ccc-a366-7203f9446eb1', '821b85b6-4ab2-4d2e-9e3d-e919f30141a6', 'This is a direct application/reinforcement of the Paper 1 add-on psychotherapy code concept — E/M (medication management) plus add-on psychotherapy code together capture this common, real-world combined psychiatric service structure, not requiring artificial separation into two visits.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('2c7636f1-1cb1-4b5f-9e4b-d787b1acfeb7', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 88, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding for psychological/neuropsychological testing (administered and interpreted by a psychologist, e.g., for cognitive assessment or ADHD evaluation), as distinguished from psychotherapy?');
VALUES ('2c7636f1-1cb1-4b5f-9e4b-d787b1acfeb7', '60ceb9ee-6551-42da-a8f4-dc8879dc459c', 'This reinforces the recurring evaluation/testing-versus-treatment coding distinction (already established for psychiatric diagnostic evaluation vs. psychotherapy, and PT evaluation vs. ongoing treatment) applied to psychological/neuropsychological testing — its own distinct, typically time-based code family separate from psychotherapy.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('31155cc4-4aad-4890-aee6-afd619ef711f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 89, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar Medicine-section code-selection question specifically involving psychiatric/behavioral health services, synthesizing this paper with Papers 1-4?');
VALUES ('31155cc4-4aad-4890-aee6-afd619ef711f', '0badebb6-fbe3-4573-9bba-abaf1c097d7c', 'This is the final Medicine-section capstone synthesis for psychiatric/behavioral health coding — connecting to the broader Medicine-section analytical discipline already established across all five papers, the same underlying approach (specific service type, participant structure, time documentation, modality) applies consistently.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('a8e04613-e21d-47e6-a1f1-2ba85d1ddacb', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 90, 'Which of the following best describes the single most important overarching lesson for CPT Medicine-section coding, as the true final synthesis across the entirety of this five-paper series'' Medicine-section content (vaccines, rehabilitation therapy, cardiovascular testing, ophthalmology, dialysis, audiology/vestibular testing, care management, and psychiatric/behavioral health)?');
VALUES ('a8e04613-e21d-47e6-a1f1-2ba85d1ddacb', '4a3d09c3-b1dc-4ba0-9e61-531aba00b89f', 'This is the true final Medicine-section capstone synthesis for the entire five-paper series — despite spanning genuinely diverse specialties, the same underlying analytical discipline (identifying specific service structure: product-plus-administration, timed-vs-untimed, evaluation-vs-treatment, participant structure, specific technique) has been demonstrated to apply consistently across every Medicine-section topic examined throughout this content.', 'Medicine — authored from standard CPT Medicine section conventions covering psychiatric therapy time-based codes; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

-- ── Section: Modifiers & NCCI (10 questions) — Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank. ──

VALUES ('78b52cc7-bfce-408b-89a6-c370256b3d91', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 91, 'Which of the following best describes the difference between an MUE''s ''claim line edit'' versus ''date of service edit'' adjudication approach?');
VALUES ('78b52cc7-bfce-408b-89a6-c370256b3d91', '2bcfccd2-8cfa-4ba8-a695-e28db42d1e23', 'This distinguishes the two MUE adjudication methodologies CMS uses — some codes are checked at the claim-line level, others aggregate units across the entire date of service — a genuine technical distinction relevant to understanding why splitting units across multiple lines doesn''t necessarily avoid an MUE edit for date-of-service-adjudicated codes.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('9cd6de85-4490-4684-ae01-531c3a206b4f', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 92, 'Which of the following best describes a compliance-relevant reason to understand whether a specific code''s MUE is adjudicated at the claim-line versus date-of-service level?');
VALUES ('9cd6de85-4490-4684-ae01-531c3a206b4f', 'ecf1eaef-7773-47bb-8d07-2cb2efa9aa6a', 'This reinforces why the claim-line-versus-date-of-service distinction has real compliance relevance — deliberately splitting units to route around an MUE edit doesn''t work for date-of-service-adjudicated codes and would itself raise a compliance concern (attempting to circumvent a payment-integrity edit) rather than reflecting a legitimate practice.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('e38e0fcd-4c60-48f4-b4f6-5b81ac4a4e59', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 93, 'Which of the following best describes an appropriate response when a claim is denied/reduced due to exceeding a code''s MUE value, and the documentation genuinely supports the higher number of units actually provided?');
VALUES ('e38e0fcd-4c60-48f4-b4f6-5b81ac4a4e59', '9c0e8d1b-5432-4304-99f3-a0d05be1e752', 'This reinforces that MUEs are payment-integrity edits designed to catch implausible unit counts, not absolute, un-appealable clinical caps — a genuinely well-documented case exceeding the MUE has an appropriate path (payer appeal process) distinct from either improperly circumventing the edit or abandoning a legitimate claim.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('25a6bcd0-f035-41ac-91a9-956de79240f1', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 94, 'Which of the following best describes the general relationship between MUE values and NCCI Procedure-to-Procedure (PTP) edits, as two distinct types of edits within the broader NCCI program?');
VALUES ('25a6bcd0-f035-41ac-91a9-956de79240f1', '63adc931-a297-4a92-8fef-e9f12ec5d1d4', 'This is a comprehensive review clarifying the MUE-versus-PTP distinction within the broader NCCI program — MUE (unit-count plausibility for a single code) and PTP (code-pair combination appropriateness) are genuinely different edit types addressing different billing-accuracy concerns, and both types can potentially apply to the same claim.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('f8cb2aab-7321-4e4d-bc6a-e33836fc0a2a', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 95, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable claim-scrubbing/compliance practice specifically for MUE-related denials, as distinguished from PTP-related denials?');
VALUES ('f8cb2aab-7321-4e4d-bc6a-e33836fc0a2a', '2a814bdb-0a82-439f-887e-e302758039e1', 'This reinforces the practical implication of the MUE-versus-PTP distinction for claims processing — correctly identifying WHICH edit type actually triggered a denial matters because the appropriate corrective response differs (modifier bypass logic applies differently to PTP edits than to MUE unit-count issues).', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('655ed56e-e2a6-40b7-88db-5c3ef9f4de09', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 96, 'Which of the following best describes correct coding when a bilateral procedure (using modifier 50, already discussed) is performed, and the specific code''s MUE value is set assuming only unilateral reporting (MUE = 1)?');
VALUES ('655ed56e-e2a6-40b7-88db-5c3ef9f4de09', 'ee7a6f42-65ff-47ae-bfe2-8a9f34d073d6', 'This acknowledges a genuinely nuanced technical interaction between bilateral modifier use and MUE unit-counting logic — rather than oversimplifying, this reinforces that coders should understand how MUE adjudication specifically accounts for (or doesn''t) bilateral-modifier scenarios for the SPECIFIC code involved, not assume a single universal rule.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('33a834bc-2f3c-487a-9b7c-90295714e6f0', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 97, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable general principle for approaching an unfamiliar Modifiers & NCCI question specifically involving MUE-related scenarios, synthesizing this paper''s MUE content with the PTP-edit and modifier content established across Papers 1-4?');
VALUES ('33a834bc-2f3c-487a-9b7c-90295714e6f0', 'cce27356-390d-4ed8-bea4-14fa38c092fc', 'This is a capstone synthesis specifically for MUE-related Modifiers & NCCI content — correctly distinguishing edit types and their distinct adjudication/resolution logic, then responding based on genuine documentation (not reflexive modifier application or arbitrary unit reduction), consistent with the broader compliance-and-accuracy discipline established throughout this content.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('fbc1f302-17ca-415d-b191-c69bb1f52979', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 98, 'Which of the following best describes a reasonable compliance program element specifically addressing MUE-related billing errors, as distinguished from general coding-accuracy training?');
VALUES ('fbc1f302-17ca-415d-b191-c69bb1f52979', '0dd6047e-f383-424d-ba02-874194ac6313', 'This reinforces the general root-cause-analysis compliance principle (already established broadly) applied specifically to MUE-related errors — targeted analysis of an organization''s own specific denial patterns can reveal genuine, addressable systemic causes (unit-counting errors, adjudication-methodology misunderstanding) that general training alone might not capture.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('74e3764b-8a07-4e1d-8805-f81e95e2087d', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 99, 'Which of the following best describes the single most important overarching lesson connecting NCCI PTP edits, MUE edits, and all modifier categories examined throughout this entire five-paper CPT series, as the true final Modifiers & NCCI synthesis?');
VALUES ('74e3764b-8a07-4e1d-8805-f81e95e2087d', '422e2916-9092-43e1-92af-5a0f4e29e729', 'This is the true, comprehensive final synthesis for the entire five-paper CPT series'' Modifiers & NCCI content — every mechanism (modifiers, PTP edits, MUE edits) shares the same fundamental purpose (accurate reflection of genuinely performed, documented work) and the same fundamental compliance risk (manipulation/circumvention rather than genuine accuracy) — the single most transferable lesson from this entire body of content.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');

VALUES ('4e8d82ea-66ac-4241-a8d7-853509334df1', 'dc8bcf93-b78b-4215-b09c-b4dcf9c4382d', 100, 'Which of the following best describes the single most important overarching lesson for the ENTIRE five-paper CPT Coding Proficiency series, spanning Evaluation & Management, Anesthesia, Surgery, Radiology, Pathology & Laboratory, Medicine, and Modifiers & NCCI?');
VALUES ('4e8d82ea-66ac-4241-a8d7-853509334df1', 'd54db941-4676-4ab5-99b7-76fcfa6819b5', 'This is the true, complete capstone synthesis for the entire five-paper CPT Coding Proficiency series — the single, transferable analytical discipline (specific-fact identification and matching to precise code descriptors) and the single, transferable compliance principle (documentation drives coding, never the reverse) have been demonstrated consistently across every section, specialty, and scenario examined throughout this entire body of content.', 'Modifiers & NCCI — authored from standard CPT modifier definitions and CMS NCCI Medically Unlikely Edit (MUE) concepts; not copied from the copyrighted CPT codebook or an official exam bank.');
